        <detaileddescription>
<para>Measures the CPU cost of the security gate that decides whether early data from a 0-RTT session is accepted or rejected:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>valid-token check (bool read)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>replay-protection check (bool read)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>This is the innermost decision point exercised on every QUIC 0-RTT resumption attempt. The gate must impose negligible latency (≤ 1 µs p99) to avoid adding meaningful overhead to the QUIC handshake fast path.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Tests both the accept path (valid, not-replayed) and the reject path (replayed) to cover both code branches. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
